  abstract = {The integration of advanced AI and machine learning (ML) technologies in small and medium enterprises (SMEs) is revolutionizing how these businesses operate, enhancing efficiency, reducing risks, and improving decision-making. By leveraging AI and ML algorithms, SMEs can automate routine tasks, optimize processes, and predict outcomes with remarkable accuracy. This includes applications such as predictive maintenance in manufacturing, real-time inventory management in retail, and personalized customer experiences in service industries. AI-driven systems can analyze vast datasets, uncover hidden patterns, and offer actionable insights that drive smarter business strategies. Moreover, ML models improve over time, adapting to new data and changing market conditions. Despite the significant benefits, challenges remain, including the need for skilled personnel, high implementation costs, and concerns over data privacy. However, with the advent of user-friendly AI tools, cloud computing, and reduced hardware costs, SMEs can now access these technologies more easily and cost-effectively. This paper explores the transformative impact of AI and ML applications in SMEs, highlighting key use cases, the benefits they offer, and the potential barriers to successful implementation.},
